# CVE-2020-1971 template completion (upstream aa0ad2011d, 1.1.1i): the
# EDIPartyName fields are DirectoryString (a CHOICE), so they must use
# EXPLICIT tags [0]/[1] (RFC 5280); 1.0.1u had IMPLICIT, which the encoder
# and decoder silently ignored. Benign known-answer test, not an exploit: a
# well-formed EDIPartyName GENERAL_NAME is built through the API, encoded and
# compared with the RFC 5280 DER (hard-coded), then decoded back and its
# fields compared. Pure library logic: same verdict on every arch.
class=kat
lib=noasan
needs_ssl=0
timeout_host=10
timeout_arm32=40
timeout_x86=10
timeout_mips=40
arm32=yes
x86=yes
mips=yes
target=yes
desc=EDIPartyName template: an API-built partyName must encode to the RFC 5280 DER (explicit [1]) and decode back into partyName
